WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.960
Pastiche recipe also
contains 60 different

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.170
herbs and spices, each
of which is separately

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.820
distilled into alcohol.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.490
One of these herbs is
Artemisia vulgaris,

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.600
commonly known as
mugwort.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.920
A worker loads mugwort
leaves into a tank filled

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.170
with a mixture of water
and alcohol.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.020
As the leaves soak, the
alcohol acts as a

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.530
solvent, extracting the
aromatic molecules.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.360
This process is called
maceration.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.640
After a few days,
workers drain the

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.520
alcoholic liquid now
infused with aromatic

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.080
molecules. It's so
alcoholic that it emits

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.490
volatile fumes.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:57.190
So workers wear an alarm
that goes off when the

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.650
surrounding air reaches
an explosive level.

